# C++ Contracts Implementation (P3850)

This fork implements the C++ Contracts extensions proposed in P3850,
building on GCC master.

The majority of the work going into the actual P2900 implementation was done
by Nina Ranns, Iain Sandoe, and Ville Voutilainen.  The additions in this
fork are all prototype-quality implementations to gain implementation
experience and explore design alternatives, though we have strived to
fix all known bugs in the upstream implementation, extend test suites
whenever possible, and are continuously working toward upstreaming
those fixes.

This branch is part of a larger project to implement Contracts features in
all open-source C++ compilers, and details on the current status and scope of
these changes can be found at https://github.com/notadragon/contracts-p3850.

## Compiler Explorer

A build of this branch is available on compiler explorer.  You can use it by
selecting the "x86-64 gcc (P3850 contracts)" entry in the compiler dropdown
when editing C++ code at https://godbolt.org/.

## Usage

All of the features can be activated with `-fcontracts-p3850`, or
`-fcontracts-p####` to enable support for a specific paper.  (Not all
variations have been thoroughly tested.)

## Known Bugs and Open Issues

Open issues with this branch are tracked in the branch itself so that
consumers have one place to go to see the current state.  Details can be
found in two distinct lists:

- open-issues/README.md -- **everything contracts-related that is known
  to be broken on this branch**, whatever its origin.  If you encounter
  issues, double-check here to see if they are known.  Some of these are
  underlying issues that we have deferred, others are in progress.
- bug-reports/README.md -- bugs that exist in the upstream trunk build
  of GCC, many of which have been fixed in this branch.

Some items that exist upstream which we have not yet fixed are in both
lists.

